 "comment": "The shop types and the shops (D-1149 to D-1155). A type holds a sale rate in basis points for each gear slot and each kind of used-up item, and a rate of 0 buys nothing of that kind (D-1151). A shop names its type and its stock. Each entry of a stock names one item, piece, or lesson, its price, and a count or `unlimited`. A lesson takes no count, and the shop hides it while the party owns it (D-1152, D-1153, D-1024). The fixture trader of the fixture hub lists the bolt, which the start pack holds, so the list hides it. PR-17 adds the trader of the mining town, which sells one step up of gear for each slot, two lessons, and the four used-up items (D-1339, D-1341). PR-30 tunes each number.",
